config BR2_PACKAGE_WIFI_HICHANNEL
	bool "HiSilicon hichannel (Hi3861L, self-boot SDIO)"
	select BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	select BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_KOPT_MMC
	help
	  Ingenic T31 port of the LuckfoxTECH hichannel/hcc driver for the
	  HiSilicon Hi3861L over SDIO (MSC1).  The chip self-boots its own
	  firmware (SPC021) from internal flash, so no host firmware download
	  is performed (unlike the wifi-hi3881 driver).

	  Requires the jzmmc host fixes in all-patches/linux/3.10.14
	  (0099 drop CMD53 CRC retry, 0100 ignore stale error irq,
	  0101 mask stale data errors for CMD52) and pull-ups on the
	  SDIO CMD/DAT0 pins (package/wifi/files/mmc_gpio_pb).

	  Also installs /usr/bin/hinl.  The chip associates and runs DHCP
	  itself; S38wpa_supplicant calls "hinl up" with the credentials
	  from /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf, and hinl copies the chip's MAC and
	  address to wlan0.  There is no AP or portal mode: set credentials
	  with "wlan configure <ssid> <password>".

	  Do not enable together with BR2_PACKAGE_WIFI_HI3881 - both drivers
	  claim the same SDIO WiFi device.
